__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Your captured stays — real dates, prices and plans, in however many databases
# you keep them in: <name>.db.json. Track these only if you mean to publish the
# trip. Left as *.json rather than *.db.json so that anything you kept under the
# old name, or off in a folder of its own, stays just as unpublished.
*.json

# Which database `db` last left you in.
.lodgingbuddy-db

# Each database's own settings — <name>.dbconf.toml, which city it's in and
# anything true of that trip alone. Yours, like the stays they sit beside.
# cities/*.cityconf.toml is the half worth committing, and isn't matched here.
/*.toml
!/config.toml
# And by name, unanchored, for the same reason the stays are: a database kept
# off in a folder of its own takes its settings with it, and the rule above
# only reaches the root — where it has to stay, so config.toml can be excepted
# from it.
*.dbconf.toml

# Built from bookmarklet.js by build_bookmarklet.py. Generate these, don't clone them.
bookmarklet.html
bookmarklet.txt
install-bookmarklet.html
